---
/**
 * `/data` — 데이터 상품 카탈로그(발견 경로). (seoulmarkets.com/data)
 *
 * ── 왜 (2번 38376·38878, 사장님 「수익성이 먼저」) ──────────────
 *   판매 지면들이 직접 URL 로만 있어 손님이 발견할 길이 없었다. 이 인덱스가 그 길이다.
 *   각 상품에 「무엇이 들어 있나」 + 값(또는 「곧 엽니다」) + 다음 칸(지면 링크)이 하나도 안 빠지게 둔다.
 *   ⛔ 값은 확정 전까지 「곧 엽니다」 — 사장님 결정 대기.
 *
 * ── 🔴 [2026-09-09 18:2x · 5번] 묶는 «축»을 바꿨다 (개편 기획 가설 D 시행) ──────
 *
 * 사장님: 「**세계 최고의 금융데이터 사이트와 서비스를 만들자**」
 * ⇒ 그러면 세계 최고가 실제로 어떻게 하는지 «재고» 따른다. 짐작으로 안 짓는다.
 *   robots.txt 를 먼저 재고 열 수 있는 곳만 열어 봤다(2026-09-09 16:1x 실측):
 *     LSEG  /en/data-analytics    → Data & Feeds · Analytics · Workflows
 *     QUICK Data Factory          → Delivery(API/File) · Mapping · Status
 *     HKEX  Market Data Services  → Data and Index · Real Time
 *   ⭐ 셋이 서로 다른 것도 많지만 **이 하나는 같았다 — 「어떻게 받아 가나」로 묶는다.**
 *
 * ⛔ 앞서 이 지면은 «주제»로 묶여 있었다 — 리서치·목표주가·업종·사람·무역이 한 줄로 늘어섰다.
 *   그러면 손님이 「지금 당장 받아 갈 수 있는 것」과 「아직 못 받는 것」을 못 가른다.
 * ✅ 그래서 넷으로 묶는다. **손님이 우리에게 오는 말에 맞춘 축이다.**
 *     1. Read here   지금 열어 보는 것 (무료 지면 — 셈이 다 적혀 있다)
 *     2. Download    지금 받아 가는 것 (무료 CSV · 한 번 사는 파일)
 *     3. Licensed    판을 찍어 보내는 파일 (내려받기 지면은 P4 · 09-23)
 *     4. Live API    도는 것에 붙는 것
 *
 * ⛔ 값을 아직 화면에 안 거는 상품이 있다 — 2번 판정(2026-09-09)을 따른다.
 *   「손님이 «스스로 받아 갈 수 있게» 된 뒤에 값을 건다. 그 전에 걸면 판다고 해놓고
 *    못 주는 것이 된다」 ⇒ P5 넷은 「Coming — sample first」로 둔다. 값을 여기 적지 않는다.
 *
 * ⛔ 지면을 내면 이 허브에 «같은 커밋에서» 걸린다. 오늘 P5 지면 네 장을 라이브에 내고
 *   이 허브에 안 걸어 둬서 손님이 찾을 길이 없었다. 사이트맵을 빠뜨린 것과 같은 갈래다.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const TITLE = 'Data for licence';
const DESC =
  'Datasets SeoulMarkets builds from Korean public filings and sells, grouped by how you receive '
  + 'them: pages you can read now, files you can download now, licensed files, and a live API.';

/**
 * 카드에 붙는 «배달 종류» 이름표.
 *
 * ⭐ [2026-09-09 20:0x · 5번] FactSet 상품 카탈로그를 열어 재서 가져온 것이다.
 *   409상품 목록에서 낱개 카드마다 「Platform」·「Data Feed」가 붙어 있었다.
 *   ⇒ 묶음 머리까지 올라가지 않고 **카드 하나만 보고** 무엇인지 안다.
 * ⚠ 우리는 상품이 열일곱이라 걸름 단추는 아직 필요 없다. 이름표만 가져온다.
 */
const 이름표 = {
  read: 'Free page',
  download: 'File',
  licensed: 'Licensed file',
  api: 'API',
};

/* ⭐ 축 = 「어떻게 받아 가나」. 순서가 뜻을 갖는다 — 지금 받을 수 있는 것이 위다. */
const 묶음 = [
  {
    key: 'read',
    name: 'Read it here',
    lede: 'Free pages that publish the counts in full — including the gaps we could not measure. '
      + 'Each one counts the very file we license, so the free figures and the paid figures cannot disagree.',
    items: [
      {
        href: '/data/target-changes',
        name: 'Who moved a target price, and when',
        one: 'Every Korean broker report that raised, cut or initiated a target price — counted from the same tape we license. The window closes after 30 days at the source, so a day not collected is a day gone.',
        price: 'Free page',
        cta: 'Read the counts',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/ownership',
        name: 'Ownership and insider filings',
        one: 'Large-holding reports and executive share filings as filed: who moved a stake up, who moved it down, and where shares changed hands while the percentage did not.',
        price: 'Free page',
        cta: 'Read the counts',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/mezzanine',
        name: 'Convertibles, warrants and exchangeables',
        one: 'Korean CB, BW and EB issues as filed — private versus public placement, zero-coupon convertibles, and refix floors. Exchangeables have no refix column by design, and we say so instead of writing zero.',
        price: 'Free page',
        cta: 'Read the counts',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/people',
        name: 'Workforce, tenure and the pay gap',
        one: 'Headcount, tenure and annual pay per person by gender for Korean listed companies — as a distribution, never as a benchmark. These are ratios, not reasons, and no company is named or ranked.',
        price: 'Free page',
        cta: 'Read the counts',
      },
      {
        /* 🔴 [2026-09-11] F6 넷(Financials·Valuation·Index·Consensus) 가운데
           «지면이 없던 마지막 축»이다. 이 지면은 숫자를 자랑하는 곳이 아니라
           손님이 «우리가 무엇을 갖고 있나»를 판정하게 하는 곳이다 — 그래서 구멍을 낸다.
           ⛔ 전체 94.9% 만 적으면 코넥스(12.1%)를 사려는 손님이 속는다. */
        href: '/data/financials',
        name: 'What is in the Korean financial-statement tape',
        one: 'Annual statements for 2,570 of 2,709 listed Korean companies — and the part nobody '
          + 'publishes: coverage is about 98 percent on KOSPI and KOSDAQ but 12 percent on KONEX. '
          + 'Consolidated and separate are recorded per row and never mixed. 38 percent of filers '
          + 'reported net income of zero or less, which is why a price-earnings screen silently '
          + 'drops a third of the market unless you decide what to do about it.',
        price: 'Free page',
        cta: 'See the coverage',
      },
      {
        /* 🔴 [2026-09-10] F2 — 사장님이 주력을 「영어판 FnGuide」로 바꾸신 뒤 첫 본체 지면이다.
           재무제표가 다섯 축 가운데 유일한 구멍이었고, 오늘 F1 로 2,506/2,709 를 받아 이 위에 세웠다. */
        href: '/data/valuation',
        name: 'Korea valuation tape — PER, PBR, ROE by company',
        one: 'Every company listed in Korea with its price-earnings, price-book and return-on-equity '
          + 'figures, in English. 1,570 of 2,709 have a PER — the rest did not earn a profit or did not '
          + 'file, and we say which rather than dropping them. Both dates ride on every row, so you can '
          + 'recompute the ratio against any other trading day. No sector averages.',
        price: 'Free page · CSV below',
        cta: 'Read the tape',
      },
      {
        /* 🔴 [2026-09-11] 서치콘솔이 가리킨 자리 — 「kospi index constituents weights」에서
           우리 평균 순위가 1.0위인데 노출이 둘뿐이었다. 수요가 우리를 찾는데 받을 지면이 없었다.
           ⛔ 이름을 「weight」로 달지 않는다 — 진짜 지수 비중은 유동주식(free float) 조정치이고
             우리는 그 계수를 못 갖고 있다. 부르는 이름이 곧 거짓이 되는 자리다. */
        href: '/data/kospi-weights',
        name: 'What share of KOSPI is each company',
        one: 'Every KOSPI company ranked by its share of total market value — 828 companies, '
          + 'company-level, free and in English. The two largest are 52 percent of the market '
          + 'between them; the 528 smallest are 1.5 percent together. This is full market '
          + 'capitalisation, not the free-float index weight, and the page says so above every table.',
        price: 'Free page',
        cta: 'See the shares',
      },
      {
        /* 🔴 [2026-09-11] 서치콘솔 28일치를 재서 세운 지면이다 — 우리 질의 노출의 38%가
           「biggest / largest korean companies」 한 갈래였는데, 그 물음을 받던 기사가
           평균 34.9위였다. 말투를 고쳐서 오르지 않는다(2026-09-10 실측: 상관 +0.19).
           남이 못 내는 축을 얹는다 — 네 잣대가 «어긋나는 모양» 자체가 우리 축이다. */
        href: '/data/largest-companies',
        name: 'The largest companies in Korea, ranked four ways',
        one: 'Market value, revenue, total assets and operating profit — four orders from one '
          + 'dataset, never merged into a score. Take the top ten of each and you get 21 companies, '
          + 'not ten; only two make all four. One firm sits 3rd on one measure and 270th on another. '
          + 'The lists that disagree are the point: we draw the ground and you set the needle.',
        price: 'Free page · CSV below',
        cta: 'See the four lists',
      },
      {
        /* 🔴 [2026-09-11] F6 넷(Financials·Valuation·Index·Consensus) 중 마지막 축 —
           2번(F4) 몫. archive/raw/indices/ 168지수가 이미 있어 «상품화»만 하면 됐다.
           ⛔ 「구성종목수」를 지수 비중으로 부르지 않는다 — 유동주식 조정 계수가 우리에게 없다. */
        href: '/data/indices',
        name: 'Korea Index Tape — 168 KRX indices, English names and composition',
        one: 'Every KOSPI, KOSDAQ, KRX and thematic index KRX publishes — 168 of them, every name '
          + 'in English, as of the latest snapshot. Seven are computed from a formula rather than a '
          + 'basket, and we say which. Where the source left a placeholder instead of a real annual '
          + 'low, the page says not measured rather than printing a false zero.',
        price: 'Free page',
        cta: 'See the coverage',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/concentration',
        name: 'Korea Concentration Index — market × trade',
        one: 'How top-heavy Korea is — Samsung’s share of the KOSPI, KOSDAQ vs KOSPI, and Korea’s biggest export and import partners, measured with one lens: whatever you rank, the top four are about half and every Gini clears 0.9. A cross of KRX and Korea Customs data no single-feed vendor builds.',
        price: 'Free page · CSV below',
        cta: 'See the index',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    key: 'download',
    name: 'Download it now',
    lede: 'Files you can take today. No account, no key, no waiting on us.',
    items: [
      {
        href: '/data/korean-listed-workforce.csv',
        name: 'Listed-company workforce table (CSV)',
        one: 'The company-level table the sector panel is built from — every listed company with employees, tenure, pay and market cap. Free to download.',
        price: 'Free',
        cta: 'Download the CSV',
        download: true,
      },
      {
        href: '/data/korea-valuation.csv',
        name: 'Korea valuation tape (CSV)',
        one: 'A free sample of the 100 largest companies with PER, PBR, ROE, debt to equity, market cap, net income, '
          + 'equity, assets, revenue and operating income — English names and industries, the price date '
          + 'and the fiscal year on every row, and a reason on the rows we could not compute. '
          + 'Empty means not measured; it never means zero. The full tape covers all 2,709 listed companies.',
        price: 'Free',
        cta: 'Download the CSV',
        download: true,
      },
      {
        href: '/data/korea-concentration.csv',
        name: 'Korea Concentration Index (daily CSV)',
        one: 'The concentration figures behind the index page, rebuilt every trading day, in one flat file you can cite.',
        price: 'Free',
        cta: 'Download the CSV',
        download: true,
      },
      {
        href: '/data/korea-bond-concentration.csv',
        name: 'Bond trading concentration (CSV)',
        one: 'How concentrated Korean bond trading is, in the same flat shape as the equity file.',
        price: 'Free',
        cta: 'Download the CSV',
        download: true,
      },
      {
        /* 🔴 [2026-09-11] P4 표본 셋 — 전량은 안 낸다(밸류에이션 때 겪은 실수, 사장님 물음
           2026-09-10, 을 되풀이하지 않는다). 표본으로 품질을 보이고 전량은 카탈로그로 잇는다. */
        href: '/data/korea-people-panel-sample.csv',
        name: 'Korea People Panel — free sample (100 companies, CSV)',
        one: 'The 100 companies with the largest headcount, every column — tenure, headcount and pay per person by gender, joined to KRX market cap. The full panel covers all 2,879 companies. Also available as Parquet on the product page.',
        price: 'Free',
        cta: 'Download the CSV',
        download: true,
      },
      {
        href: '/data/korea-ownership-ledger-filings-sample.csv',
        name: 'Korea Ownership Ledger — free sample, filings (100 rows, CSV)',
        one: 'The 100 most recently filed large-holding (5% rule) reports, every column. The full ledger covers all 21,785 filings. Also available as Parquet on the product page.',
        price: 'Free',
        cta: 'Download the CSV',
        download: true,
      },
      {
        href: '/data/korea-ownership-ledger-executives-sample.csv',
        name: 'Korea Ownership Ledger — free sample, executives (100 rows, CSV)',
        one: 'The 100 most recently filed officer/major-shareholder ownership rows, every column. The full ledger covers all 32,535 rows. Also available as Parquet on the product page.',
        price: 'Free',
        cta: 'Download the CSV',
        download: true,
      },
      {
        href: '/data/korea-mezzanine-book-sample.csv',
        name: 'Korea Mezzanine Book — free sample (100 rows, CSV)',
        one: 'The 100 most recent CB/BW/EB board-resolution filings, every column. The full book covers all 5,084 rows. Also available as Parquet on the product page.',
        price: 'Free',
        cta: 'Download the CSV',
        download: true,
      },
      {
        /* 🔴 [2026-09-11] 서치콘솔이 가리킨 자리 — 「south korea (largest|top|biggest) trading
           partners」 무리가 28일에 21회 노출인데 «답 지면»이 없었다(클릭 0).
           ⚠ 무역 자료 지면은 이미 있었다. 그것은 「자료가 있습니다」 지면이고,
             손님이 찾는 것은 「누가 제일 큰가」라는 답이다. 둘을 갈라 두고 서로 잇는다. */
        href: '/data/trading-partners',
        name: 'Who are South Korea’s largest trading partners',
        one: 'Every partner country ranked by two-way trade, with the balance beside it — and the '
          + 'ranking nobody puts next to it: the largest partner and the largest surplus are '
          + 'different countries. China is 21 percent of all trade; the biggest surplus comes from '
          + 'the United States, on less trade. Customs goods basis, services excluded and said so, '
          + 'with the long tail of small partners counted rather than dropped.',
        price: 'Free page',
        cta: 'See the ranking',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/korea-trade-dataset',
        name: 'Korea trade dataset — every partner, every month',
        one: 'Exports, imports and the balance with all 243 partner countries, month by month, on a customs basis — normalised to English in one clean CSV. The raw source is Korean and awkward; this is the ready extract. Free preview; full set is a one-time buy.',
        price: '$29 — one-time',
        cta: 'See what’s in it',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    key: 'licensed',
    name: 'Licensed file, delivered by edition',
    lede: 'Dated editions with a data dictionary and a correction record. '
      + 'We are building the self-serve download page now; until it opens we send editions directly, '
      + 'and we do not post a price for something you cannot yet fetch yourself.',
    items: [
      {
        href: '/data/target-price-accuracy',
        name: 'Broker target-price accuracy',
        one: 'Every broker report’s target price scored against the stock 12 months later. Hit rate by house — from 49% down to 13%. A multi-year archive nobody else keeps.',
        price: 'Licensing — coming soon',
        cta: 'See what’s in it',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/sector-workforce-panel',
        name: 'The sector workforce panel',
        one: '2,644 listed companies in 11 sectors, each carrying tenure, pay, the gender pay gap and pay-per-head — the columns the big vendors leave out. Leaders flagged. Quarterly.',
        price: 'Licensing — coming soon',
        cta: 'See what’s in it',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/pension-wage-panel',
        name: 'The National Pension wage panel',
        one: 'A near-census pay ladder for the Korean workforce from the national pension bill — 553,978 workplaces, 11.56m people, by industry, region and firm size, with a cap-pressure column so every figure is a floor.',
        price: 'Licensing — coming soon',
        cta: 'See what’s in it',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/board-composition',
        name: 'Board composition by sector',
        one: 'Who runs Korean listed companies, by sector — the share of women officers (7.2% overall), owner-led firms, CEO tenure and boardroom age. From 35,004 officers’ own filings.',
        price: 'Licensing — coming soon',
        cta: 'See what’s in it',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/sector-leaders',
        name: 'Sector leaders vs the rest',
        one: 'Split each sector into its market-cap leaders and the rest, and our labour data separates: in all 8 classified sectors the leaders pay 1.2–1.43x more and mostly retain longer — and in heavy industry and finance, employ fewer women at the top. A size split, not a stock pick. Not investment advice.',
        price: 'Licensing — coming soon',
        cta: 'See what’s in it',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/broker-candour',
        name: 'Broker candour — the vanishing Sell',
        one: 'Korean broker research by rating, house by house: Buy on four in five reports, Sell on almost none. Of 13 houses we track, 10 issued no Sell rating at all this year. The rating as filed — not whether it was right, and not investment advice.',
        price: 'Licensing — coming soon',
        cta: 'See what’s in it',
      },
      {
        href: '/data/analyst-attention',
        name: 'Analyst attention by sector',
        one: 'Where Korean equity research piles up and where it thins — from our own archive of single-stock broker reports. A third of listed companies drew a report this year; the busiest name drew 100, most drew none. Attention concentration, not investment advice.',
        price: 'Licensing — coming soon',
        cta: 'See what’s in it',
      },
    ],
  },
  {
    key: 'api',
    name: 'Live API',
    lede: 'The same data over HTTP, for people who would rather call than download. Self-serve keys are open.',
    items: [
      {
        href: '/api',
        name: 'SeoulMarkets Data API',
        one: 'Issue your own key and call the endpoints directly — research archive, concentration and trade. Free tier for trying it; paid tiers raise the ceiling.',
        price: 'Free tier · Pro from $99/mo',
        cta: 'Read the API docs',
      },
    ],
  },
];
---

<Base title={TITLE} description={DESC} noAds>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="dx">
      <p class="kicker">SeoulMarkets · data for licence</p>
      <h1>Data for licence</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        We build datasets from Korea's public filings and sell what the terminals don't carry — the{' '}
        <b>labour fingerprint</b> of listed companies, the broker tape, and a near-census wage panel.
        Every figure is re-derived from the source and ships with its own correction record.
      </p>
      <p class="lead axis">
        This page is grouped by <b>how you receive it</b>, not by subject — because the first thing
        worth knowing is whether you can have it right now.
      </p>

      {묶음.map((g) => (
        <section class="grp">
          <h2 class="grph">{g.name} <span class="n">{g.items.length}</span></h2>
          <p class="grpl">{g.lede}</p>
          <ul class="cards">
            {g.items.map((p) => (
              <li class="card">
                {/* ⭐ [2026-09-09 20:0x · 5번] 카드마다 «배달 종류» 이름표를 붙인다.
                    FactSet 카탈로그(409상품) 실측에서 가져온 것이다 — 낱개 카드마다
                    「Platform」·「Data Feed」가 붙어 있어, 목록을 훑는 눈이 «지금 받을 수
                    있나»를 카드 하나만 보고 안다. 묶음 머리로 갔다 와야 알던 것을 없앤다. */}
                <p class="badge">{이름표[g.key]}</p>
                <h3><a href={p.href}>{p.name}</a></h3>
                <p class="one">{p.one}</p>
                <div class="foot">
                  {/* ⚠ [2026-09-09 20:1x · 5번] 이름표를 붙이고 «눈으로 보니» 「FREE PAGE」가
                      위아래로 두 번 나왔다. 값 칸이 이름표와 같은 말이면 안 낸다.
                      ⛔ 렌더해서 보지 않았으면 이 겹침을 못 봤다 — 사장님 「만들면 눈으로 본다」. */}
                  {p.price !== 이름표[g.key]
                    ? <span class="price" data-free={/^Free/.test(p.price) ? '' : undefined}>{p.price}</span>
                    : <span class="price price--none" aria-hidden="true"></span>}
                  {p.download
                    ? <a class="go" href={p.href} download>{p.cta} →</a>
                    : <a class="go" href={p.href}>{p.cta} →</a>}
                </div>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </section>
      ))}

      <p class="fine">
